>> title: Injera
>> category: Flatbreads & Pancakes
>> tags: teff, ethiopian, fermented, griddle, vegan
>> counters: Shawarma Counter
>> aka: enjera, injeera, taita, Ethiopian flatbread
>> pairs-with: doro-wat
>> servings: 10
>> time: 3 days
>> slack: unforgiving — three days of wild fermentation is the whole bread and it is judged by smell and bubble rather than by the clock: stopped early it is flat batter with no sour in it, left too long it goes sharp and bitter, and neither can be pulled back to the middle
>> step.3: ferment 3 days at room temperature
>> step.5: pour in a spiral, cover, steam 3 min

Whisk @teff flour{3%cup}(390 g; ivory or brown teff), @barley flour{1/2%cup}(60 g), and @water{5%cup}(1.2 L) into a thin batter.

Stir @ersho{1/4%cup}(60 mL; starter from the last batch, or 1/2 tsp instant yeast) into @&(~1)batter{}.

Ferment @&(~1)batter{} covered at room temperature ~{3%days}, until it smells sour and a clear liquid sits on top.

Whisk @&(~1)fermented batter{} with @fine sea salt{1%tsp}(6 g), @warm water{1/2%cup}(120 mL).

Pour @&(~1)batter{} in a spiral onto a hot #mitad{}, cover, and steam ~{3%min}.
